{
  "description": "`each` runs its body once per addressed turtle, and every entry creates a fresh scope with fresh bindings (spec/execution-model.md:377-379,664-666), so the second turtle's pass must not find the `:carried` the first bound — `ol-undefined-var` (spec/error-model.md:102). `:seen` is born outside the `each` and so is one binding all passes update, which is what lets the body count its own passes without depending on the property under test. The sibling `sprites/each-body-is-a-block-scope` pins that a name born in the body dies at the `]`; a body given ONE scope hoisted out of the per-turtle loop passes that fixture unchanged, because the single frame still ends with the statement. Added at the QA reviewer's request during the review gate, which built that implementation — plausible because `ask` legitimately pushes one scope, having no loop — and measured it surviving all 1029 fixtures.",
